@@ -22,4 +22,12 @@ operation fails, including a failed `test`. A patch is atomic: on error nothing
 Removing the whole document (`remove` with an empty path) is rejected, as is moving a value into its
 own child.
 
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns
+the merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated. An object patch is merged into the
+target member by member (a non-object target is treated as `{}`), a `null` member removes that member,
+and any other patch value, arrays included, replaces the target wholesale. It never throws: every
+JSON value is a valid patch. `null` cannot be set as a value, as the RFC specifies.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs the TypeScript tests directly).
